======================================================================
Design a schematic for A simple circuit to drive a small OLED display for status information. Use exactly these real components: D1, and C1 as 2 separate instances of a D_Small (Generic small-footprint diode), R1 as a 1N4148 (Small-signal fast-switching diode, 100 V 200 mA, through-hole), U1 as a LCD-016N002L (16x2 character LCD module with HD44780 controller. 16-pin interface.). Do not substitute or invent a different part for any of them. Wire it up as follows: connect U1's VDD pin (pin 2) to R1's A pin (pin 2); connect U1's VSS pin (pin 1) to R1's K pin (pin 1) to D1's A pin (pin 2); connect U1's RS pin (pin 4) to D1's A pin (pin 2); connect U1's E pin (pin 6) to D1's K pin (pin 1); connect U1's RW pin (pin 5) to D1's K pin (pin 1); connect U1's LED+ pin (pin 15) to D1's A pin (pin 2).

